<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
  The icon the Android 12+ splash screen draws: deliberately nothing.

  From API 31 the system shows a splash for every cold start whether or not the
  app asks for one, and the default is the launcher icon over the window
  background. The bundle then plays its own logo animation — the mark arriving,
  settling and lifting — so the default put a static copy of the same mark on
  screen a moment before the animated one, and the cut between them read as a
  flash.

  There is no attribute for "no icon". Handing the platform a fully transparent
  drawable is the way to get one: the splash still runs, with nothing in the
  icon slot, so all the player sees is `windowSplashScreenBackground` — the
  same blue the window and the WebView are already painted — straight into the
  animation.

  Below API 31 there is no system splash and this is unused; `windowBackground`
  covers that case on its own.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="@android:color/transparent" />
</shape>
